  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Flood Disaster in Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan is the eighth country in the world most vulnerable to climate change and is prone to multiple disasters including floods and earthquakes, which are major recurrent disasters that have in the past caused huge losses to life and property and bared a huge socio-economic cost. Since mid-June 2022, up to 33 million people have been affected by severe monsoon weather, with an area-weighted rainfall of 67 per cent above normal levels - equivalent to 2.9 times the national 30-year average. The storms and heavy rains have caused widespread flash floods and landslides, with severe repercussions for human lives, property, and infrastructure. To date, 80 districts across Pakistan&apos;s five of six provinces have been declared &apos;calamity hit&apos; by the Government of Pakistan. Through this project, IOM is contributing towards the provision of emergency shelter and non-food item (NFI) assistance for populations affected by the floods in Pakistan. To this end, IOM is developing an intervention focused on the shelter and NFI sector that will be implemented in Balochistan, Sindh, and Khyber Pakhunkhwa provinces, the three most affected provinces by the floods.</narrative>
  </description>
